cmnf5wnfe000kuxs39wfd29si	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	conversion. Coercion is done automatically and can sometimes lead to unexpected results or subtle\nbugs.\nExample in C:\nint x = 5; float y = 2.5; float result = x + y; // x is coerced from int to float\nautomatically // result = 7.5\nHere, the integer x is coerced to 5.0 before addition. Another classic example: in JavaScript, "5" + 3\nyields "53" (string concatenation) due to coercion, while "5" - 3 yields 2 (numeric subtraction) — an\ninconsistency that confuses many developers.	[-0.016714472,0.005902204,0.011739006,-0.07084552,-0.0029185351,0.014943036,0.0048515517,0.014032706,0.012647478,-0.016153602,-0.01404368,3.479185e-05,-0.012620831,-0.023818176,0.1504852,0.0027139336,-0.0071703317,0.0048984294,0.017815832,-0.00173392,0.0055408156,0.0061950935,-0.012257747,-0.018095419,-0.017728396,-0.008427804,0.005685647,-0.0074573867,0.043574587,-0.0017955416,-0.019028664,0.010043377,0.006992657,0.019788932,-0.033828795,0.006269621,0.012521254,0.011885069,0.026437845,0.01111498,0.0016720943,0.022029322,0.0048387162,-0.012068117,-0.014884019,0.030470543,-0.0065169097,-0.0064393305,-0.019259661,0.002223443,0.020094315,0.011740491,0.010362869,-0.20753764,-0.00953153,-0.0052195066,-0.0006878585,0.0028657427,0.021950742,0.004243624,0.011771337,0.02550605,0.0065428545,0.009514193,0.014388304,0.0056237136,0.04420456,0.016688757,-0.035447497,-0.010225813,0.023473706,0.00066718116,-0.018965684,-0.019931233,0.0037532388,-0.020587046,0.016783431,-0.017102228,-0.018605866,0.01777299,-0.021146668,-0.02355422,-0.00475854,-0.030194629,-0.011631197,0.009763234,-0.0057695033,-0.0059522768,0.004596235,0.0070099747,0.012562599,-0.010012049,0.002487055,0.02327314,0.0016085538,-0.0075132693,-0.011777399,0.021903425,-0.00788015,-0.014583886,0.015161422,-0.015449524,-0.0057515614,0.0046954136,-0.021118503,-0.006147689,0.005931568,0.0008513829,-0.005695104,0.0040698196,0.00639762,-0.022194115,0.013133394,0.0012213644,0.008514727,-0.1954567,0.