cmnf5wnti000luxs37jhc8mf4	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	Languages can be weakly typed (allow extensive coercion, like JavaScript) or strongly typed\n(restrict coercion, like Python 3), affecting how safe and predictable programs are.\nQ8. Explain binding and binding time spectrum with example.\nA binding is an association between a name (like a variable or function) and a property (like its type,\nvalue, or memory address). The moment in a program's lifecycle when this association is\nestablished is called the binding time.\nThe Binding Time Spectrum (from earliest to latest)\n1. Language Design Time: Some bindings are fixed when the language itself is designed.\nExample: the meaning of the + operator for integers is bound at language design time — it always\nmeans addition.\n2. Language Implementation Time: Bindings determined by the compiler/interpreter\nimplementation. Example: the size of an int in C (16, 32, or 64 bits) is decided by the\nimplementation.	[-0.0042646583,0.0054172995,0.0023162137,-0.05158258,-0.00012777913,0.015970845,0.016105127,0.007493999,0.008306434,0.0102903405,-0.0078008235,-0.004136544,-0.0030266675,0.0012852256,0.124893546,0.0072100135,-0.027120562,-0.009414066,0.021514509,-0.0074092844,0.0038920997,0.025661906,-0.005490013,-0.020120624,-0.007994594,-0.014201325,0.012125824,0.0011981943,0.043994416,-0.0089086685,-0.021294788,0.018650055,0.0063266847,0.045753676,-0.0020623659,0.018623568,0.003306868,-0.008285026,0.015871199,0.009961287,-0.019847682,-0.0005734363,0.018156199,0.008261628,-0.007854405,0.019911936,-0.0027037377,-0.01903191,-0.03990929,0.02724026,0.006691741,0.011249766,-0.009934751,-0.18456306,0.0027888042,-0.02092981,-0.006139254,0.010874604,0.0052246926,0.00694035,-0.01157414,-0.005817646,-0.025670609,0.011248677,0.031431176,-0.0015803772,0.02357591,0.006394949,-0.016212527,-0.0017802027,0.012036612,0.006860373,0.0009919537,-0.008601743,0.0063245893,-0.015112673,0.018570937,-0.0415563,-0.005513637,0.018670907,-0.011417059,-0.004