cmnf5wo8n000muxs3evte4hy7	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	2. Language Implementation Time: Bindings determined by the compiler/interpreter\nimplementation. Example: the size of an int in C (16, 32, or 64 bits) is decided by the\nimplementation.\n3. Compile Time: Bindings established when the source code is compiled. Example: the type of a\nstatically declared variable in Java — int count; binds the type integer to count at compile time.\n4. Link Time: When separately compiled modules are linked together. Example: the address of a\nfunction defined in another file is bound during linking.\n5. Load Time: When the program is loaded into memory. Example: the actual memory address of a\nglobal variable is bound when the OS loads the program.\n6. Runtime: Bindings that occur during execution. Example: in Python, the type of a variable is\nbound at runtime — x = 5 binds integer to x, but later x = "hello" rebinds it to string. Early binding\n(compile time) is more efficient; late binding (runtime) is more flexible.	[-0.008377483,0.008168892,-0.0017697816,-0.061218392,-0.0073417565,0.017336976,0.0050737034,0.0020986018,0.009740954,0.006425255,-0.0021835575,0.003814531,-0.010450462,-0.01210232,0.13385662,0.0064087873,-0.014906057,-0.008814362,0.020347267,-0.015253836,-0.0067190076,0.01212304,-0.011640522,-0.025625128,-0.0089751035,-0.008690866,0.018044328,0.013328298,0.045726642,-0.010244882,-0.018220322,0.037526384,0.028391115,0.026384713,-0.006003192,0.019774346,-0.000989971,-0.032406542,0.013193032,0.004710283,-0.0018353948,0.0030702893,0.030214649,0.01337112,-0.010499074,0.034464844,-0.008446564,-0.0062969066,-0.03707124,0.027884638,0.004454005,0.0073298565,-0.0043526045,-0.20213209,0.008014805,-0.023428716,-0.0040214146,0.019398715,-0.003995308,0.010681346,-0.006652874,-0.0023446435,-0.019577568,-0.0006578517,0.03424721,-0.02097747,0.02221658,-0.009310813,-0.019745195,-0.0004723373,-0.00381045,0.012440999,-0.0053477376,-0.0084038805,-0.009022696,-0.02731862,0.0042982274,-0.02