cmnf5wrz0000tuxs30n6gadxr	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	1. Reduces complexity: Developers using a module only need to understand its interface, not its\ninternals. This reduces cognitive load significantly.\n2. Prevents unintended interference: External code cannot corrupt the internal state of a module,\nleading to more reliable programs.\n3. Enables independent development: Different teams can develop different modules concurrently\nas long as interfaces are agreed upon.\n4. Facilitates change: Internal implementation can be improved or fixed without breaking external\ncode that depends on the module.\n5. Promotes encapsulation: It reinforces the encapsulation principle — keeping data and the\nmethods that operate on it together and protected.\nQ12. Explain the concept of classes and objects in programming languages with\nsuitable example.\nClass\nA class is a user-defined blueprint or template that defines the attributes (data members) and\nbehaviors (methods) that objects of that class will have. A class is like a cookie cutter — it defines	[-0.0026169475,-0.0039440147,0.016246032,-0.06133422,-0.0039301133,0.0099006975,0.0325855,0.023565592,0.02755647,-0.005545463,-0.007198741,-0.017164053,-0.0055501624,0.008523487,0.12998931,0.009359692,-0.011449734,-0.004892911,0.01984529,-0.028287582,0.015330503,0.01361507,0.002483843,-0.019160299,0.00069251977,1.2930461e-06,0.0047827247,0.0128113935,0.054297965,-0.013299832,-0.011729859,0.032668717,0.014202588,0.027305355,-0.0042905044,0.0002140046,0.0020480163,-0.0017953772,-0.004018178,0.0074030263,-0.012984987,-0.0074029164,0.00419996,0.015327241,0.011916311,0.011218948,0.008496107,-0.009093737,-0.013144855,0.01648579,0.018462777,-0.0065848143,-0.00018828845,-0.1959072,0.030651696,-0.0035956125,-0.0031974502,0.010355395,0.0019141138,-0.0043373397,-0.0055412618,-0.0003504819,-0.012667519,0.012071308,0.0008684233,-0.030778242,0.018875886,-0.015310804,-0.014497267,0.008395968,0.013525723,0.0029634268,-0.0080253165,-0.011259766,0