cmnf5wtrb000wuxs36ujd63rd	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	Character: Represents a single character using encoding (ASCII or Unicode). Example: char grade\n= 'A'; in C.\nString: While technically a class in many languages (like Java), strings are treated as primitives in\nsome languages (e.g., Python, JavaScript). Example: str name = "Alice";.\nPrimitive types have fixed sizes, support direct operations (arithmetic, comparison), and are\nstored by value (not reference) in most languages.\nQ14. Explain the concept of structured data types in programming languages.\nStructured data types (also called composite or aggregate data types) are data types constructed\nfrom two or more primitive or other structured types. They organize related data together under a\nsingle name, making it easier to manage complex information.\nCommon Structured Data Types\nArrays: A collection of elements of the same type stored in contiguous memory locations, accessed\nby an index. Example: int scores[5] = {90, 85, 78, 92, 88}; — a sequence of 5 integers.	[-0.014746886,-0.004761363,0.009105472,-0.062213812,-0.021536559,0.02671776,0.016816989,0.012013994,0.024203373,0.021341654,-0.009784733,-0.00746026,-0.004501695,-0.0049241916,0.12868755,-0.009356275,-0.013538589,-0.008537939,0.0217317,-0.028659243,0.008914515,0.014867531,-0.0154030025,-0.018455558,-0.010380058,-0.02128288,0.0018843855,0.007593868,0.032975156,-0.008962094,-0.01568969,0.012413998,0.0057277773,0.013642748,-0.020588977,0.00071649917,-0.009926134,-0.0048965844,0.0014106715,0.017613947,-0.00074890134,-0.017501505,-0.0011695514,-0.0043977997,0.0038828843,0.020286469,0.013012909,-0.0016298109,-0.033220712,0.027637048,0.012154093,0.0006648083,-0.016592978,-0.2049495,0.03645468,0.007325695,-0.002330572,0.017986856,0.0042752307,-0.000153119,0.005031386,0.007191709,-0.0016041711,0.017608732,0.013752575,-0.00942838,0.024784757,0.010477717,-0.005409131,0.004780672,0.024162846,-0.0068123075,-0.0065079904,-0.015754059,0.0064284727,-0.013273875,