cmnf5wviw000zuxs3fknkc5ji	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	C++ achieves this with templates, Python uses duck typing (implicit parameterization). Type\nparameterization is fundamental to the Standard Template Library (STL) in C++ and Java\nCollections Framework.\nQ16. Explain the concept of modules and packages in programming languages.\nModules\nA module is a self-contained unit of code that groups related functions, classes, variables, and\nconstants together. Modules promote separation of concerns, code reuse, and namespace\nmanagement. Each module has its own scope, preventing name collisions. In Python, any .py file is\na module. In Java, a class file serves a similar role.\nExample in Python: a module named math_utils.py could contain functions like add(), multiply(), and\nfactorial(). Another file imports it with import math_utils and uses math_utils.add(3, 4).\nPackages\nA package is a collection of related modules organized in a hierarchical directory structure.	[-0.0011871393,0.0037696273,0.00029367153,-0.051483266,-0.014786931,0.01553265,0.020744292,0.020459197,0.017598102,-0.0032352626,-0.0119809825,-0.0018719524,-0.016622968,0.004074757,0.12460369,0.0062222984,-0.0025695858,-0.012814259,0.026306042,-0.028260665,0.0078028464,0.012447455,-0.0046981806,-0.023044625,-0.0012800202,-0.011166098,0.009407092,0.0014306853,0.047715586,-0.0008243133,-0.016060475,0.026935497,0.016425136,0.018827815,-0.014894315,0.00030844728,-0.013392307,-0.012787543,0.013782257,0.018320818,-0.012047088,-0.0067822807,0.008350635,0.009012434,-0.0057963934,0.001262925,0.0023428379,-0.00800498,-0.044742566,0.014243084,0.013918542,0.0006848184,0.0040617967,-0.18526216,0.017172659,-0.0070874062,-0.0037350124,0.014112303,0.025844818,-0.002928803,-0.005836211,0.012009427,-0.027978372,0.0032309573,-0.0017005713,-0.021120103,0.036970854,-0.01256269,-0.014497712,-0.011333917,0.0032044873,0.0077360747,-0.003828128,-0.014442609,0.016065374,-0.0041485764,0.025579335,-0.027921943,-0.0008734937,0.023497