cmnf5wyaa0014uxs32eid95wf	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	Perl with local) use dynamic scoping.\nVisibility\nVisibility is related to scope but focuses on whether a particular declaration of a name is accessible\nat a given point. A variable may be in scope but hidden (not visible) because a local declaration of\nthe same name shadows it.\nExample:\nint x = 10; // global scope void foo() { int x = 20; // local x — shadows global x\nprintf("%d", x); // prints 20 (local x is visible) } // After foo(), global x = 10 is\nagain visible\nCommon scope types include: global (entire program), local (within a function/block), class (within\na class), and module (within a module).\nQ19. What is inheritance? Explain with example.\nInheritance is a fundamental object-oriented programming mechanism that allows a new class\n(called a subclass or derived class) to inherit the attributes and methods of an existing class\n(called a superclass or base class). This promotes code reuse, establishes an 'is-a' relationship	[-0.0027786496,0.0055531175,0.0175067,-0.06260391,-0.025913237,0.016511958,0.0042377906,0.015906293,0.028364029,-0.008277712,0.0010865822,-0.010570185,-0.021896813,-0.008033007,0.117212124,0.0011303328,-0.027725123,-0.0029704773,0.018257085,-0.009519034,0.007767463,-0.00290213,7.188374e-05,-0.02088616,0.013808263,0.007541636,0.0064872145,0.015811203,0.05210327,0.005909757,-0.0053805523,0.038486153,0.01273147,0.009868498,-0.0141457375,0.00861438,0.011329868,-0.0039892606,-0.0018082742,-0.0022828507,-0.029890819,0.000829968,0.0013068028,0.0016446192,0.00306875,-0.0036839866,0.0036020752,-0.019277988,-0.03231164,0.00384768,0.015084682,0.011312162,-0.0066701984,-0.19805418,0.0015962191,-0.0015890115,0.004172291,-0.0013087076,-0.010476254,-0.003264176,0.0031791297,-0.000538891,-0.00034746088,-0.0037406483,0.011677824,-0.018775284,0.018458256,-0.00020718528,-0.020692972,0.0030350187,0.01151874,0.004908582,-0.011087779,-0.0032942707,-0.0034326024,-0.011667872,0.0014721397,-0.0398499