cmnf5wynp0015uxs39z6pgi6o	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	(called a subclass or derived class) to inherit the attributes and methods of an existing class\n(called a superclass or base class). This promotes code reuse, establishes an 'is-a' relationship\nbetween classes, and supports hierarchical classification.\nThe subclass can reuse inherited members, override inherited methods to provide specialized\nbehavior, and extend the superclass with new attributes and methods.\nExample in Java:\nclass Animal { // Superclass String name; void breathe() { System.out.println(name + "\nbreathes."); } } class Dog extends Animal { // Subclass — inherits from Animal void\nbark() { System.out.println(name + " says: Woof!"); } void breathe() { // Method\noverriding System.out.println(name + " breathes through lungs."); } } Dog d = new\nDog(); d.name = "Rex"; d.breathe(); // Calls Dog's overridden version d.bark(); //\nDog's own method\nTypes of Inheritance\nSingle inheritance (one parent), multiple inheritance (multiple parents — supported in C++, Python),	[-0.005135236,0.013430748,0.019037765,-0.06507013,-0.018853266,0.016214076,0.0021039818,0.0014034214,0.030269897,-0.0010305571,-0.0030956746,-0.008813262,-0.014523728,-0.0070329946,0.1365402,-0.016594298,0.0007875007,-0.014904767,0.004707044,-0.02500907,0.0043100566,-0.004627107,0.015944649,-0.018436527,0.0005838587,0.016130898,-0.001528681,0.026902424,0.043618903,-0.0044631027,-0.015931765,0.037047833,0.011671423,0.003022866,-0.025495892,-0.0022397235,0.014508079,-0.00091237825,-0.012670405,-0.0021808906,-0.004741857,0.021962281,-0.007215132,0.001458334,0.00035618735,-0.005830993,0.0055393265,-0.015679654,-0.014633585,0.008388976,0.00861221,0.011476059,-0.010283029,-0.2447105,0.0030275583,0.0071650012,-0.004631486,-0.011663781,0.00531269,0.01246533,-7.179721e-05,0.0048186006,0.0049379203,0.0047392035,0.022797948,-0.028570917,0.026771024,0.0088810045,-0.013094104,0.019403769,0.013183693,0.013414256,-0.0024507542,-0.0023355049,0.009859