cmnf5wzew0017uxs3dh1ngu6d	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	Data abstraction and information hiding are closely related and complementary principles. Together\nthey form the foundation of modular, maintainable software design. Here are their combined and\nindividual advantages:\n1. Reduced Complexity: By exposing only the essential interface and hiding implementation\ndetails, these principles significantly reduce the complexity that any programmer needs to\nunderstand at one time. A developer using a HashMap doesn't need to know about hash functions\nor collision resolution.\n2. Increased Modularity: Systems built on abstraction and hiding naturally decompose into\nindependent modules. Each module can be developed, tested, and debugged in isolation, making\nlarge-scale software engineering feasible.\n3. Ease of Maintenance and Modification: Since implementation details are hidden, internal\nchanges (e.g., switching from a bubble sort to a quicksort) do not affect other parts of the system	[-0.0064148894,-0.0049240887,0.02186548,-0.059270997,-0.005614305,-0.0010065145,0.020315899,0.026082067,0.0073746284,-0.0055540767,-0.011868298,0.005676132,-0.00048321238,0.0022841105,0.11444873,0.007454032,0.014854935,-0.007920622,0.010514916,-0.026651714,0.02188637,0.015555132,-0.002003887,-0.03517761,0.0003688734,0.005139171,0.008554324,0.006690244,0.03185868,0.0016128992,-0.001666538,0.027926337,0.0053910012,0.023408117,0.0045433994,-0.00012781844,0.0022461512,0.01300406,-0.0025685704,0.0057574008,0.01324495,0.01677858,0.008916605,0.0028684556,0.0074055865,0.01575046,0.009734007,-0.006479367,-0.0208914,0.0047219363,0.022833772,-0.014952387,-0.006565675,-0.20530838,0.023560975,0.0054145497,-0.0074404613,0.006460374,0.008271757,0.012724225,-0.010555768,0.019986883,-0.020398486,0.011974423,0.006494424,-0.02974003,0.012611612,-0.013180194,-0.026590237,0.024554817,0.018956417,0.0035295205,-0.023667831,0.0011175423,0.023456784,0.0014204832,0.004127648,-0.008398412,0.00055856677,-0.000338533