cmnf5wzs40018uxs36pno0pph	cmnf5wccs0003uxs3mc5evhul	3. Ease of Maintenance and Modification: Since implementation details are hidden, internal\nchanges (e.g., switching from a bubble sort to a quicksort) do not affect other parts of the system\nthat depend on the abstracted interface. This is known as the Open/Closed Principle.\n4. Enhanced Reusability: Well-abstracted components with clean interfaces can be reused across\ndifferent projects. For instance, Java's Collections library is reused in millions of applications\nworldwide.\n5. Improved Security and Integrity: Information hiding prevents external code from accessing and\npotentially corrupting internal data. For example, making a bank account's balance field private\nensures it can only be modified through controlled methods that enforce business rules.\n6. Better Encapsulation: Bundling data with operations that act on it, and restricting access, leads\nto objects that are self-managing. This models real-world entities more naturally.	[-0.0022589944,-0.003012999,0.022105202,-0.06458086,-0.0025181763,0.001972923,0.022500334,0.033064675,-0.0023095838,-0.006214236,0.0062722503,0.005445905,-0.0031709142,-0.0028361965,0.120820545,0.005462475,0.019082839,0.00013125902,0.010657283,-0.025407584,0.018030271,0.014976375,0.003539161,-0.03137062,0.0006041163,0.0057854997,0.0057154754,0.009422643,0.036751535,-0.006629477,-0.015286881,0.03511359,0.025491916,0.018442191,0.007196076,0.0021260786,0.007009719,0.003557903,-0.009447258,-0.008770495,0.0061857193,0.008425445,0.0035993434,0.0003553238,-0.0043984987,0.0053572627,0.0016932247,-0.022941062,-0.012035707,0.0101448335,0.015312849,-0.010856558,0.0038485369,-0.21966621,0.026463833,0.010811012,-0.0026480756,-0.005130009,0.017012043,0.012277972,0.006986924,0.024853794,-0.0012079112,0.00904821,0.0030656448,-0.040098667,0.013450028,-0.016031403,-0.022918627,0.017396605,0.006691482,0.013240919,-0.021575997,2.082615e-05,0.027408639,-1.5577058e-05,0.008114985,-0.00036324625,0.0